    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d746">

                <pb facs="0838" n="644" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg644"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">864.918/7–1745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 746<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative in Hungary</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Schoenfeld</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d746-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Budapest</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-17T16:00:00+02:00">July 17, 1945—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>297. Gregoriev[,] Pushkin’s Assistant[,] has asked Balogh for list Hungarian newspapermen
                    previously correspondents wholly or in <pb facs="0839" n="645" xml:id="pg645"/>
                    part for foreign newspapers and who will presumably engage in reporting
                    subsequent to reestablishment international communications. This is first
                    evidence Russians will raise blackout on foreign correspondents but there are no
                    indications they will permit uncontrolled reporting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Schoenfeld</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d746-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d746-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this message was included in telegram No. 65 of July 19 from
                        Grew to Byrnes (file No. 800.00 Summaries/7–1945).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
